**How to implement.** One fit: a study, a stage and a calibration use in; one fit run out, stamped by the clock (001 §P `RunFit`; 001 §E 'Fit runs are append-only and store the full parameter vector they used and produced'; the S11.3 brief 'The stamp comes from ClockProvider', 'A run holds the full parameter vector used and produced, the mode and stage, the data hashes it read, and notes'). The fit computes; writing is the job's, on completion only (step 393). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, last: (1) `StudyFitRequest = { study : StudyName; stage : FitStage; calibrationUse : CalibrationUse }`, what `RunFit` asks (Run joint is `JointStage`, Run stage `CalibrationStage` or `ObjectStage`, S11.5). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitParam = { forward : StudyForwardContext; clock : ClockProvider; linearSolver : MuellerSolverProxy; deviates : UniformDeviateProvider; fitRuns : FitRun list }` (the `*Param` convention): the kit as the study sees it (step 372), the clock (step 122), the SVD proxy, the deviates (step 339) and the study's fit runs as the kit last read them (step 384). (3) `type StudyFitParam with member this.runFit (request : StudyFitRequest) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>`: the study of `this.forward.kit.studies` named by the request (else the new `UnknownFitStudyErr of reason : string`, rendered `the kit has no such study: <reason>`); its `stageWith this.forward.kit request.stage request.calibrationUse` (step 385, an error `FitStageErr`); over the context with `kit.items` replaced by the staged items, the staged study's `prefitWith` (step 377) of `fitted`, the `dataRead` of the latest of `this.fitRuns` of that study by stamp (empty before its first), and its `dataWith` (step 378), an error `StudyForwardFitErr`; the engine `engineWith` chooses (step 386), `calibrateLinear` for a linear `CalibrationStage`, `reconstructLinear` for any other linear stage, and `fitNonlinear` (with the watch) otherwise (steps 387-390); then `this.clock.now ()`, read once, and the `FitRun` (step 383): `schemaVersion` current; `name` the study name's `fitRunNameAt` that instant and `stamp` the instant; `mode` the study's `settings.mode`; the request's stage and calibration use; the solution's engine; `runs` the staged study's `fittedRuns`; `dataRead`, for each prefit whose experiment carries data, in order, its attachment's path at the hash the fit read: `current` of a `ChangedSinceAttachFlag` or `ChangedSinceFitFlag` and the attachment's own hash for `DataUnchangedFlag` (step 370); `parameters`, every parameter of every staged item `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` the fitted runs (step 261), item by item in their order, as `ItemParameterRef` with its state, then every component of every opened material of the staged study as `MaterialParameterRef` with its state; `entries`, the layout's entries with the start vector's and the solution's fitted values; the solution's members and object matrices; and `FitRunNotes.none`. Nothing is written here. No other member or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`: `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced`: step 387's polarimeter study through a `StudyFitParam` whose clock answers 2026-11-04 09:30:00 UTC and whose `fitRuns` are empty, `runFit` of `JointStage` and `CalibrationHeldFixed` unwatched, answers the run named `<the study's stem>@20261104T093000Z` at that stamp, `JointFit`, `JointStage`, `CalibrationHeldFixed`, `NonlinearStudyEngine`, its plate run as the one fitted run, its attachment's path at its hash as the one `dataRead`, the opened material's four components with their states among its parameters, n_o's and n_e's entries with their starts and fitted values equal to `fitNonlinear`'s, and one member. The same fact MUST additionally drive the valid partial-matrix fixture from step 390 (only m33 fixed, all instruments and gains fixed) through `runFit` under both `ObjectStage` and `JointStage` with `CalibrationHeldFixed`. Each request MUST complete a real SVD solve and return a `LinearStudyEngine` FitRun, fifteen fitted entries recovering the synthetic truth within 1e-9, m33 unchanged with its known state in `parameters` and absent from `entries`, and a complete `ObjectMatrixFit` with rank 15. This MUST exercise automatic dispatch rather than calling `reconstructLinear` directly or accepting a pre-fit error; `a fit naming no study of the kit, or refused by its stage, records nothing`: a request naming `LR`, which the kit lacks, answers `UnknownFitStudyErr`, and `ObjectStage` over step 385's study with CPL1 uncalibrated `FitStageErr (InstrumentNotCalibratedErr _)`. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case. Extend the existing fit-run fact to drive every new step 390 case through runFit under both ObjectStage and JointStage. The ideal-CP m00 cases MUST produce LinearStudyEngine runs of rank 1 and one fitted entry. Equality-linked cases MUST produce one fitted entry per independent leader, preserve full parameter snapshots with followers resolved consistently, and produce complete matrices satisfying the links. Use a recording linear proxy that delegates to the real SVD; an unexpected nonlinear solve or an earlier error MUST fail the fact.

**Acceptance.** After the fit lands, `StudyFitParam.runFit` MUST stage the study, check and read its data, choose and run the engine and answer a `FitRun` stamped by the clock holding the runs, the data hashes, every parameter read and the vector used and produced, writing nothing; with only m33 fixed and the instruments and gains fixed, both object-stage and joint requests MUST automatically run the linear solver, recover the fifteen free coefficients within 1e-9, preserve m33 exactly and record reduced rank 15; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced` and `a fit naming no study of the kit, or refused by its stage, records nothing`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass. Automatic dispatch MUST also complete the ideal-CP m00 and equality-linked fixtures in both requested stages using the real linear solver, recording independent fitted entries, resolved followers and the reduced rank.
